<title>DENMARK: Danish May yr/yr CPI up 1.9 pct (EU method).</title>
<headline>Danish May yr/yr CPI up 1.9 pct (EU method).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices were 0.6 percent higher in May 1997 from April 1997 and 1.9 percent up on May 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The CPI data was issued under EU-harmonised calculation methods. Under the traditional Danish national formula the respective figures would have been a 0.7 percent month-on-month rise and 2.1 percent up year-on-year.</p>
<p>	  EU FORMULA		 May 1997   April 1997    May 1996</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)    +0.6	 +0.3	    +0.2</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)     +1.9	 +1.5	    +1.6</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	 102.0	 101.4	   100.1</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)    +0.7	 +0.3	    +0.4</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)     +2.1	 +1.7	    +1.9</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	 204.1	 202.7	   200.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' average expectations were for a 1.9 percent yr/yr rise from May 1996 according to the national formula. -- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
